ion (B2) over infectious/malignant processes, and provide weak support against autoimmune blistering disease. The absence of inflammatory markers and systemic symptoms maintains a lower probability for VZV and malignant vascular involvement."}, {"timestep": 4, "bundle_id": 4, "bundle_position": 3, "bundle_size": 7, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Could the absence of fever, tachycardia, or constitutional symptoms (E6, E8) in a 39-year-old with rash (E2) undermine the plausibility of acute HSV-1/HSV-2 infection (B1.1) in favor of non-infectious vascular proliferation (B2)?", "result_summary": "The patient's normal vitals and lack of dermatomal distribution reduce the likelihood of VZV compared to HSV-1/2, moderately support benign vascular proliferation (B2) over infectious/malignant processes, and provide weak support against autoimmune blistering disease. The absence of inflammatory markers and systemic symptoms maintains a lower probability for VZV and malignant vascular involvement."}, {"timestep": 4, "bundle_id": 4, "bundle_position": 4, "bundle_size": 7, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of neurological signs, localized pain, or dermatomal distribution in the case (E6-E11) contradict the likely pattern of shingles (VZV) and favor non-specific vesicular viral or autoinflammatory causes?", "result_summary": "The patient's normal vitals and lack of dermatomal distribution reduce the likelihood of VZV compared to HSV-1/2, moderately support benign vascular proliferation (B2) over infectious/malignant processes, and provide weak support against autoimmune blistering disease. The absence of inflammatory markers and systemic symptoms maintains a lower probability for VZV and malignant vascular involvement."}, {"timestep": 4, "bundle_id": 4, "bundle_position": 5, "bundle_size": 7, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of documented autoimmune signs (no arthritis, SLE-like rash, or mucosal involvement) in the patient's exam (E6-E9) disfavor autoimmune blistering disease as an explanation?", "result_summary": "The patient's normal vitals and lack of dermatomal distribution reduce the likelihood of VZV compared to HSV-1/2, moderately support benign vascular proliferation (B2) over infectious/malignant processes, and provide weak support against autoimmune blistering disease. The absence of inflammatory markers and systemic symptoms maintains a lower probability for VZV and malignant vascular involvement."}, {"timestep": 4, "bundle_id": 4, "bundle_position": 6, "bundle_size": 7, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "What evidence is MOST INCONSISTENT with Benign Vascular Proliferation? Identify the single strongest finding that argues against this diagnosis.", "result_summary": "The patient's normal vitals and lack of dermatomal distribution reduce the likelihood of VZV compared to HSV-1/2, moderately support benign vascular proliferation (B2) over infectious/malignant processes, and provide weak support against autoimmune blistering disease. The absence of inflammatory markers and systemic symptoms maintains a lower probability for VZV and malignant vascular involvement."}], "differential_history": [{"B1": 0.47976307996051337, "B2": 0.3998025666337612, "B3": 0.07107601184600199, "B4": 0.0246791707798618, "B5": 0.0246791707798618, "B1.1": 0.29985192497532087, "B1.2": 0.14992596248766044, "B1.3": 0.02998519249753209}, {"B1": 0.298207759632112, "B2": 0.3932410017126752, "B3": 0.01941930872655186, "B4": 0.013485631060105458, "B5": 0.013485631060105458, "B1.1": 0.1966205008563376, "B1.2": 0.08192520869014065, "B1.3": 0.019662050085633757}, {"B1": 0.28384648299740184, "B2": 0.4893123729244916, "B3": 0.006712103880994399, "B4": 0.009322366501381109, "B5": 0.004661183250690554, "B1.1": 0.24465618646224582, "B